# sdl-linux-x86_64

The generic hosted x86-64 board with its screen and pointer moved into a
window. Everything else is inherited: the same SDK, the same MCU, RTC and IMU
providers, and the same named device map.

Two bindings naming one provider module is deliberate rather than a shortcut.
SDL has one video subsystem and one event queue, so one module implements both
interfaces and registers both objects, and binding it twice is how a board says
that both roles are served by the same thing.

Selecting this board uses SDL2 for display and touch. An application importing
mm.audio also links SDL2 for audio on any Linux board.
The SD socket binding reports Unsupported because this SDL board has no card.
